# Authority Boundary Audit

```yaml
rules:

  - id: ARA_001
    name: BUILDER_CANNOT_CERTIFY_OWN_ARTIFACT
    description: >
      CTO/Coder CANNOT certify their own build.
      Certification requires independent validation.
    enforcement: ALWAYS

  - id: ARA_002
    name: TESTS_ARE_OWNED_BY_CSA
    description: >
      Validation scripts MUST be owned by CSA.
      No self-certification allowed.
    enforcement: ALWAYS

  - id: ARA_003
    name: STUB_IMPLEMENTATION_CANNOT_PASS_CERTIFICATION
    description: >
      Stub implementations MUST NOT pass certification.
      Real file reading required for GGUF.
    enforcement: ALWAYS

  - id: ARA_004
    name: HARD_CODED_OUTPUT_IS_VIOLATION
    description: >
      Hardcoded output (e.g., "qwen2", tensor_count: 291)
      without file dependency is STUB violation.
    enforcement: ALWAYS

  - id: ARA_005
    name: EVERY_ARTIFACT_HAS_OWNER
    description: >
      Every artifact MUST declare owner in canon.
    enforcement: PRE_COMMIT

  - id: ARA_006
    name: EVERY_ARTIFACT_HAS_AUDITOR
    description: >
      Every artifact MUST have CSA validation script.
    enforcement: POST_BUILD

  - id: ARA_007
    name: EVERY_FEATURE_HAS_CERTIFICATION_PATH
    description: >
      Every feature MUST have defined certification path.
    enforcement: PRE_COMMIT

  - id: ARA_008
    name: AUTHORITY_BEFORE_EXECUTION
    description: >
      Authority check BEFORE execution.
      FAN Registry lookup REQUIRED.
    enforcement: RUNTIME

boundary_check:

  pre_commit:
    - Run FAN Registry lookup
    - Check ASI for integration path
    - Validate Hookpoint boundary

  post_build:
    - CSA audit script execution
    - Validation against golden fixtures
    - Authority chain verification

  runtime:
    - FAN::resolve(feature) -> owner
    - IF owner != consumer: DELEGATE
    - IF no FAN: FAIL
```